00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:59.240
When share count falls and earnings stay stable, earnings per share and book value per share both rise mechanically,

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:04.660
even if net income is flat, because the same earning stream is divided across fewer shares.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:10.400
That only holds if the repurchase price stays below the intrinsic value the market later assigns.

00:09:10.800 --> 00:09:16.140
Divide the announced repurchase cap by current shares outstanding to see the maximum percentage reduction,

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:20.280
then compare that percentage against the common equity tier one target.

00:09:20.840 --> 00:09:24.900
If the ratio stays comfortably above regulatory minimums after the buyback,

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:27.860
the capital return is credible rather than cosmetic.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:35.120
